# Master control (Supabase only)

Master accounts are **not** self-service. Enable access and assign a **unique 6-digit PIN per master** in SQL only.

## 1. Enable master control for an account

```sql
UPDATE public.profiles p
SET master_control = 'yes'
FROM auth.users u
WHERE p.id = u.id
  AND lower(coalesce(u.email, '')) = lower('your-master@email.com');
```

Sign out and sign back in so `master_control` loads in the app.

## 2. Set that account’s master PIN (unique per user)

The hash uses `PIN + user_id + 'dalton_master_v1'`. **Each master account must have its own PIN.**

Replace `YOUR_6_DIGIT_PIN` and the user id (or use the email join):

```sql
UPDATE public.profiles p
SET master_pin_hash = encode(
  digest(trim('YOUR_6_DIGIT_PIN') || p.id::text || 'dalton_master_v1', 'sha256'),
  'hex'
)
FROM auth.users u
WHERE p.id = u.id
  AND lower(coalesce(u.email, '')) = lower('your-master@email.com')
  AND p.master_control = 'yes';
```

The app only **verifies** this PIN (Settings → Master intake / Master control). PINs cannot be changed from the app after migration `019`.

## 3. Remove master access

```sql
UPDATE public.profiles
SET master_control = 'no', master_pin_hash = null
WHERE id = '<profile-uuid>';
```

## 4. Deploy master PIN verification (fixes REST 404 on `verify_master_pin`)

From the repo root (requires Supabase CLI + `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` secret):

```bash
supabase functions deploy verify-master-pin --project-ref txehbzyntvqpkkegjrwp
```

The app calls this Edge Function instead of the PostgREST RPC. Redeploy after changing PIN logic.

## 5. Proposal follow-up emails

Deploy Edge Function `submit-proposal-followup` and set:

- `RESEND_API_KEY`
- `PROPOSAL_TEAM_EMAIL` — comma-separated inboxes for Dalton review (e.g. `you@domain.com,partner@domain.com`)

In-app master alerts on new proposals use DB trigger `trg_notify_masters_new_proposal` plus optional `notify-masters-proposal` for push/email.
